  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Script interpreter: A/Y is the address of a script. Each opcode byte selects a routine in script_ops. Opcode $ff ends the script, or returns from a script call. An opcode with bit 7 set takes its operands from the argument stack in place of the script."},
    {"at":3,"placement":"line","text":"Jump table entry: read_bitmap_byte."},
    {"at":6,"placement":"line","text":"Jump table entry: read_cell_colour."},
    {"at":9,"placement":"line","text":"Saves A/Y in script_ptr and clears the loop stack, the return stack and the argument stack."},
    {"at":21,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the next opcode. $ff: end or return. Else run the opcode routine."},
    {"at":34,"placement":"line","text":"Opcode $ff: return to the calling script when script_return_stack has an entry, else end."},
    {"at":56,"placement":"line","text":"Gets one operand in A: pops it from script_arg_stack when script_stack_mode is not 0, else reads the next script byte."},
    {"at":60,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the byte at script_ptr in A and increments script_ptr. Y = 0."},
    {"at":71,"placement":"line","text":"Pops the top byte of script_arg_stack in A. Y = the new script_arg_index."},
    {"at":80,"placement":"line","text":"Runs the routine of opcode A: bit 7 goes to script_stack_mode, bits 0-6 select the entry of script_ops. The opcode routine returns to the interpreter loop with RTS."},
    {"at":97,"placement":"side","text":"Jumps to the address in temp_word. Op 9 also comes here."}
  ],
